// draft-native-reading-run.bml — the body reads its own drafts: the covenant as data, then its own voice, one line each.
//
//   ./fkwu observe/draft-native-reading-run.bml </dev/null        the oldest pending draft
//   echo '{"count":6}' | ./fkwu observe/draft-native-reading-run.bml
//
// The drafts are the ones observe/prompt-draft-run.bml writes; pending here means no native reading follows a draft's latest
// path row, whatever we read of it (a second reader beside observe/draft-reading-run.bml, whose list moves on our readings alone). Each
// is read as form-stdlib/bml/draft-native-reading.bml says: the covenant (model/fixtures/draft-reading/covenant.jsonl, graded
// by observe/alignment-read-run.bml as a cell in its grading lane, a named path judged against the tree at the draft's time),
// then, when every covenant predicate holds, the reviewing voice the governor's room allows with rp-sema in front, one ask per
// draft. Rejected whenever a covenant predicate fails, without asking the voice; else the voice's word. Each reading lands in
// receipts/draft-ledger.jsonl as the reading row (form-stdlib/bml/draft-ledger.bml) with "reader":"native-voice", the predicate
// tally and the voice's account after it. Prints one line per draft as it lands or is refused, the voice's line, and answers the summary line.
// stdin, optional, one JSON object (door-options: a malformed line or an unknown key is refused by name):
//   count          how many of the oldest pending drafts to read (default 1)
//   ids            read these drafts (any reading state) in place of the oldest pending; an id the ledger holds no draft
//                  for is refused by name
//   newest         1 takes the newest pending first (the walk's: a draft with the turn before under the current packet can teach; of the
//                  oldest unread read first on 2026-10-31, none became an accepted row)
//   until_ms       a time on host_monotonic_ms: an ask begins only with its floor left before it (the walk's window)
//   ledger         the draft ledger (default receipts/draft-ledger.jsonl)
//   covenant       the covenant rows (default model/fixtures/draft-reading/covenant.jsonl)
//   tree           the checkout whose git history answers what stood at a draft's time (default this one)
//   voice_lines    a JSONL of {"draft","line"} read in place of the voice (the band's lane: no model opens; a row may name
//                  "status" for a voice that did not answer); its lines are fixtures, so it reads only beside a scratch ledger
//                  named by ledger, and beside receipts/draft-ledger.jsonl it is refused by name
//   model          a registry name for the voice (default the review role when the governor has room for it, else the
//                  fast-answer role, else no voice and the door says why)
//   work           where the grader's fixture files, its evidence and each packet and voice answer are kept
//                  (default .hearth/draft-native-reading)
//   covenant_only  1 grades the covenant alone: no voice, nothing lands
// A physical reading needs the GPU; expect a minute or more per ask while it is shared. rent_tokens 0.
// preflight-exec: forbidden
import form-stdlib/bml/draft-native-reading.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/stdin-source.bml;
section [form.bml] {
 dnr-run(dop-doc(dnr-door(), stdin-text(), dnr-spec()));
}
